              382239,
              99128,
              507162,
              548231
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 382239,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Thanks for setting this up. The color-coding is great. However, view-only access will be a bottleneck for the sales team. We need to be able to block out tentative slots for client visits ourselves, which can then be confirmed by an assistant. Can we adjust the permissions?",
            "mentions": [
              425046
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 548231,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "I agree. A better workflow would be to allow account managers to 'propose an event'. This keeps them empowered but maintains central control for confirmation, preventing the scheduling conflicts mentioned in the project risks.",
            "mentions": [
              382239
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 425046,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "That makes sense. I can change the settings to allow that. So, the rule will be: Sales can create 'tentative' events, and an assistant must review and change them to 'confirmed'. Are we all in agreement on this structure?",
            "mentions": [
              382239,
              548231
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
